Restore the MAX_LINE_LENGTH build-time override for the FPM access log buffer.

PHP 8.4 dropped this #ifdef in php/php-src@9c267778 ("FPM: Remove usage of
non-existing MAX_LINE_LENGTH constant", php/php-src#5634) on the assumption
that nothing ever defined the constant. We do: build/Dockerfile passes
-DMAX_LINE_LENGTH=8192 through PHP_CFLAGS so that access log lines are not
truncated at 1024 bytes with "the log buffer is full (1024)".

This restores the pre-8.4 behaviour verbatim, so the buffer size stays driven
by PHP_CFLAGS for 8.2, 8.3 and 8.4 alike.

PHP 8.5 replaced this fixed buffer with zlog streams bounded by the runtime
"log_limit" setting, so this patch is specific to the 8.4 branch and must not
be carried forward.

--- a/sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_log.c
+++ b/sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_log.c
@@ -19,7 +19,11 @@
 #include "fastcgi.h"
 #include "zlog.h"
 
-#define FPM_LOG_BUFFER 1024
+#ifdef MAX_LINE_LENGTH
+# define FPM_LOG_BUFFER MAX_LINE_LENGTH
+#else
+# define FPM_LOG_BUFFER 1024
+#endif
 
 static char *fpm_log_format = NULL;
 static int fpm_log_fd = -1;
